599 they fall below their plateau (C3 302.6 vs 308.7). In the next block, 12600–13199, the drop is much deeper (C3 272.9 °C, C4 116.8, C6 112.5, C7 113.0, C8 107.3). They then recover from 13200 onwards. A joint drop like this is not the slow upward drift of a normal batch run.\n3. **Placing the onset inside 12000–12599.** C3 averages about 6 °C below plateau over that block. If it fell suddenly to the ~273 °C level of the next block, that works out to roughly the last 100 s of the block, around second 12500. If it fell gradually instead, the onset would be earlier, so I chose 12450. The small dip in C4 (120.32 vs 120.55) fits a late-block start.\n\nThe scoring rules ask for interval ends I have data for. The only such points here are the map edges, 12000 and 12600, and that gap is 600 s, wider than the 240 s limit. So I'm reporting a point answer, even though it is inferred from block averages rather than raw seconds."}, {"type": "tool_use", "id": "toolu_01VnEVCTi9kNqSX7RjFpifUG", "name": "report", "input": {"state": "anomalous", "onset": {"kind": "point", "second": 12450}, "evidence": [{"channel": "C3", "start": 12000, "end": 12599, "observation": "600 s mean drops to 302.6 from a plateau of about 308.7"}, {"channel": "C3", "start": 12600, "end": 13199, "observation": "deep drop to 272.9, then recovery"}, {"channel": "C4", "start": 12000, "end": 13199, "observation": "falls with C3: 120.3, then 116.8"}, {"channel": "C6", "start": 12600, "end": 13199, "observation": "falls together with the other heaters (112.5)"}, {"channel": "C8", "start": 12600, "end": 13199, "observation": "falls together with the other heaters (107.3)"}], "cause": "All heater temperatures (C3, C4, C6, C7, C8) dip together, which points to a disturbance in heating power; the current flag reflects the recovery afterwards"}, "caller": {"type": "direct"}}], "container": null, "stop_reason": "tool_use", "stop_sequence": null, "stop_details": null, "usage": {"input_tokens": 2818, "cache_creation_inp